<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg micro-ocellus wavelength of Drosophila guttifera at 2.12 µm (Drosophila guttifera)",
        "Schnakenberg micro-ocellus wavelength of Drosophila guttifera at 2.12 µm faithfully reproduces Drosophila guttifera morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila guttifera specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila guttifera" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Werner 2010 published this PDE.",
        "does_not_claim: That anisotropy 3.15 or heteroneura a=0.24 was measured. Spieth 1981 is a head-shape paper.",
        "does_not_claim: That the global dark-blob count of 28 equals the 16 named wing spots.",
        "does_not_claim: That the terminal GIF frame is a 2.12 µm micrograph. It is the adult photograph; the generative field is the preceding frames and the comparison figure.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Fixed-band spectral centroid on cycles [0.30, 0.80] and the equal-diffusion ablation.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Grimshawi anisotropy 3.15 and heteroneura basal activator 0.24, as chronospecies contrasts at 0 Ma.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: One campaniform Gaussian (a_w=0.12) on the guttifera morphology run.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters a=0.10, b=0.90, Du=0.016, Dv=1.25, with the spatial unit chosen so λ(k_max)=2.12 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: Koseki, Tanaka & Koshikawa 2021: wingless is expressed in specific campaniform-sensillum cell types.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979: diffusion-driven instability and the two-species reaction used here.",
        "reported_in_source: Werner et al. 2010: Wingless at vein intersections and campaniform sensilla induces yellow melanin spots on the D. guttifera wing.",
        "transfer_boundary: Sibling slot 3011 is the ~102 µm whole-wing spot scale. This patch is the interior of one spot.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 2.12 µm figure is the campaign detail tier, not a length reported by Werner et al. 2010." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila guttifera (Polka-Dotted 16-Spot Wing Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-guttifera-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_guttifera_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila guttifera; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Werner et al. 2010: Wingless at vein intersections and campaniform sensilla induces yellow melanin spots on the D. guttifera wing. | Koseki, Tanaka & Koshikawa 2021: wingless is expressed in specific campaniform-sensillum cell types. | Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979: diffusion-driven instability and the two-species reaction used here.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg parameters a=0.10, b=0.90, Du=0.016, Dv=1.25, with the spatial unit chosen so λ(k_max)=2.12 µm. | One campaniform Gaussian (a_w=0.12) on the guttifera morphology run. | Grimshawi anisotropy 3.15 and heteroneura basal activator 0.24, as chronospecies contrasts at 0 Ma. | Fixed-band spectral centroid on cycles [0.30, 0.80] and the equal-diffusion ablation.; transfer_boundary: The 2.12 µm figure is the campaign detail tier, not a length reported by Werner et al. 2010. | Sibling slot 3011 is the ~102 µm whole-wing spot scale. This patch is the interior of one spot.; does_not_claim: That Werner 2010 published this PDE. | That anisotropy 3.15 or heteroneura a=0.24 was measured. Spieth 1981 is a head-shape paper. | That the terminal GIF frame is a 2.12 µm micrograph. It is the adult photograph; the generative field is the preceding frames and the comparison figure. | That the global dark-blob count of 28 equals the 16 named wing spots.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 